cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TOPTEXT, its ideas or its code, please cite it using the
  preferred citation below (the preprint).
type: software
title: "TOPTEXT: Topological Text Analysis via Embedded Flow Graphs"
abstract: >-
  TOPTEXT is a model for topological text analysis based on so-called
  flow graphs. Its architecture has a built-in distinction between syntax
  (horizontal structure, generated by the individual sentences of a text)
  and semantics (vertical structure, generated by lexical recurrence or
  semantic fields). The flow graph embeds in a two-dimensional oriented
  surface; its boundary cycles replace the parameter-dependent windows of
  distributional semantics and allow transparent and interpretable
  algorithms for topic modeling and focus detection. The model is
  particularly suited to literary, scientific and philosophical texts.
